{title: I have come into the world as light}
{subtitle: John 12:46}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 70}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [F/A] | [Gm7] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Eb]For they loved hu[Bb]man glory [F/A]more
Than the glory of [Gm]God
Then [Eb]Jesus cried out
Who[Bb/D]ever believes in [F]me
[Gm]Does not believe in me
But in [Eb]him who sent me
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Bb]I have come into the world [F/A]as light
[Gm]So that no one who believes [Eb]in me
[Bb]Should re[F]main in dark[Eb]ness
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
And if anyone [Bb]hears my [F/A]words
And does not keep [Gm]them
I [Eb]do not judge him
For I [Bb]did not come to judge [F]the world
[Eb]But to save the world
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Gm]Whoever rejects me
And [F]does not receive my words
Already [Eb]has a judge
[Gm]The very word I have [F]spoken
Will [Eb]judge him on the last day
{end_of_bridge}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Bb]I have not spoken on my [F/A]own authority
[Gm7]The Father has com[Eb]manded me
{end_of_verse}
